{
  "name": "JsonIsItemsKind",
  "comment": "A json value is item's, not text's (ruling 2, decisions 773 + 774). A json value can\nhold any value (a number, a bool, a list, a dict), so its parent is item, not text: a\nvalue carrying Type={item, kind: json} lands as an item whose kind navigates as the\n\"json\" type (ruled by 774 — a kind's name is its name under its parent), and `%x% is\ntext` is false. Written in formal so the builder's Type choice is out of it. Red today:\ntype.name reads \"text\" (stage 3 fixes it); `is text` fires so %isText% reads true\nagainst the expected null (stage 3 fixes it); %x!type.kind.name% reads null — stage 4\nmakes a json value hold its raw text until first use, and the kind navigates then.",
  "step": [
